<article class="env-lemma" id="0DYI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DYI">Lemma <span data-tag="0DYI">15.103.4</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $I \subset A$ be an ideal. Let $K \in D(A)$ be pseudo-coherent and let $M$ be a finite $A$-module. For each $p \in \mathbf{Z}$ there exists an $c$ such that the image of $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits _ A^ p(K, I^ nM) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits _ A^ p(K, M)$ is contained in $I^{n - c}\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits _ A^ p(K, M)$ for $n \geq c$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a bounded above complex $P^\bullet $ of finite free $A$-modules representing $K$. Then $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits _ A^ p(K, M)$ is the cohomology of 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(F^{-p + 1}, M) \xrightarrow {a} \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(F^{-p}, M) \xrightarrow {b} \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ A(F^{-p - 1}, M)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       and $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits _ A^ p(K, I^ nM)$ is computed by replacing these finite $A$-modules by $I^ n$ times themselves. Thus the result by Lemma <a href="/tag/0G3K" data-tag="0G3K">15.103.1</a> (and much more is true). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>